      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a draft for the **Getting Started** guide that prioritizes readability and logical flow over artificially inflating heading counts. It uses clear, concise sections with meaningful bullet points to explain the core concepts of CloudScale DataStream.\n\n### Getting Started with CloudScale DataStream\n\nCloudScale DataStream simplifies real-time data ingestion and processing by providing a lightweight, interoperable API. Before you begin, ensure your integration environment has active SSL/TLS support and that your application identity is properly registered within the CloudScale portal.\n\n#### 1. Authentication\nAuthentication is required for every request to ensure security and access control. You can obtain a valid session token by using the POST `/v1/auth/login` endpoint with your registered API credentials.\n*   **Method:** Send a `Authorization` header containing your Bearer token.\n*   **Token Expiry:** Tokens are valid for 24 hours unless specified otherwise in your subscription plan.\n\n#### 2. Connecting to the Stream\nOnce authenticated, establish a connection to your specific data stream instance to start sending or receiving payloads. Use the RESTful `GET` endpoint on the stream identifier to retrieve connection metadata and status.\n*   **Endpoint:** `POST /v1",
